{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-69-1","title":"Psalms 69:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 David complains of his affliction. 13 He prays for deliverance. 22 He devotes his enemies to destruction. 30 He praises God with thanksgiving.</p>\n<p>(Title.) Shoshannim. 45:1; 60:1; 80:1; *titles A Psalm.It is uncertain when this Psalm was composed; though it is probable that it was written by David during the rebellion of Absalom. It is an exceedingly fine composition; it evidently refers to the advent, passion, and resurrection of our Lord, to the vocation of the Gentiles, and the reprobation of Jews: See the Marginal References.</p>\n<p>the waters. 2,14,15; 18:4; 42:7; Isa 28:17; 43:2; La 3:54; Jon 2:3-5 Re 12:15,16; 17:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-2","title":"Psalms 69:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>I sink. 40:2; Jer 38:6,22 deep mire. Heb. the mire of depth. deep waters. Heb. depthof waters. 88:6,7; Eze 27:26-34 the floods. 32:6; Ge 7:17-23; Mt 7:25; 26:37,38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-3","title":"Psalms 69:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I am. 6:6; 13:1-3; 22:2; Heb 5:7 my throat. 21; 22:15; Joh 19:28 mine. 119:82,123; De 28:32; Job 11:20; 16:16; Isa 38:14; La 2:11 I wait. 25:21; 39:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-4","title":"Psalms 69:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>hate. Joh 15:25; 1Pe 2:22 more than. 40:12 being. 7:3-5; 35:12,19; 38:19,20; 109:3-5 then I. Isa 53:4-7; 2Co 5:21; 1Pe 2:24; 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-5","title":"Psalms 69:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>and my sins. Heb. and my guiltiness. 17:3; 19:12; 44:20,21 hid. 38:9; Jer 16:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-6","title":"Psalms 69:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Let not. 7:7; 25:3; 35:26; Isa 49:23; Lu 24:19-21; Ac 4:7 O God of Israel. 72:18; 2Sa 23:3; Ac 13:17,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-7","title":"Psalms 69:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Because. 22:6-8; 44:22; Jer 15:15; Joh 15:21-24 shame. Isa 50:6; 53:3; Mt 26:67,68; 27:29,30,38-44; Lu 23:11,35-37 Heb 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-8","title":"Psalms 69:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>become. 31:11; Job 19:13-19; Mt 26:48-50,56,70-74; Joh 1:11; 7:5 and an alien. 1Sa 17:28; Mic 7:5,6; Mt 10:21,22,35,36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-9","title":"Psalms 69:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>zeal. 119:139; 1Ki 19:10; 1Ch 15:27-29; 29:3; Mr 11:15-17; Joh 2:14-17 and the. 89:50,51; Ro 15:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-10","title":"Psalms 69:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>102:8,9; 109:24,25; Lu 7:33,34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-11","title":"Psalms 69:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I made. 35:13,14; Isa 20:2; 22:12; Joe 1:8,13 I became. 44:13,14; De 28:37; 1Ki 9:7; Jer 24:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-12","title":"Psalms 69:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>They. De 16:18; Mt 27:12,13,20,41,42,62,63; Lu 23:2; Ac 4:26,27 I was. 35:15,16; Job 30:8,9; Mr 15:17-19 drunkards. Heb. drinkers of strong drink. Da 5:2-4,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-13","title":"Psalms 69:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>my prayer. 55:16,17; 91:15; Mt 26:36-46; Lu 22:44; Joh 17:1-26; Heb 5:7 1Pe 2:23 in an. 1Sa 25:8; Es 5:2,6; 7:2; Isa 49:8; 55:6; 2Co 6:2 in the. 40:10,11; 98:3; Ge 24:27; Mic 7:20; Lu 1:72; Ac 13:32,33; Ro 15:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-14","title":"Psalms 69:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>Deliver. 40:1-3; Jer 38:6-13; La 3:55 let me. 25:18,19; 35:19; 109:3,21; Lu 19:14,27; Ac 5:30,31 out of. 1,2,15; 42:7; 124:4,5; 144:7; Mr 14:34-42; 15:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-15","title":"Psalms 69:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>waterflood. Isa 43:1,2; Jon 2:2-7; Mt 12:40; Re 12:15,16 pit. 16:10; 88:4-6; Nu 16:33,34; Ac 2:24,31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-16","title":"Psalms 69:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>for thy. 36:7; 63:3; 109:21 turn. 25:16; 26:11; 86:15,16; Mic 7:19 according. 13; 51:1; Isa 63:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-17","title":"Psalms 69:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>hide. 13:1; 22:24; 27:9; 44:24; 102:2; 143:9; Mt 27:46 for I am. Mt 26:38 hear me speedily. Heb. make haste to hear me. 40:13; 70:1; Job 7:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-18","title":"Psalms 69:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>Draw. 10:1; 22:1,19; Jer 14:8 redeem. 31:5; 111:9; Job 6:23 because. De 32:27; Jos 7:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-19","title":"Psalms 69:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>my reproach. 7-9; 22:6,7; Isa 53:3; Heb 12:2; 1Pe 2:23 dishonour. Joh 8:49 mine. 2:2-4; 38:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-20","title":"Psalms 69:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Reproach. 42:10; 123:4; Heb 11:36 I am. 42:6; Mt 26:37,38; Joh 12:27 I looked. Isa 63:5; Mr 14:37,50 take pity. Heb. to lament with me. but there. 142:4; Joh 16:32; 2Ti 4:16,17 comforters. Job 16:2; 19:21,22; Mt 26:56</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-21","title":"Psalms 69:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>gall for my meat.Bochart, from a comparison of this passage with Joh 19:29, thinks that {rosh} is the same herb as the evangelist calls [ ,] hyssop; a species of which, growing in Judea, he proves from Isaac ben Orman, an Arabian writer, to be so bitter as not to be eatable. Theophylact expressly tells us, that the hyssop was added [ ,] as being deleterious, or poisonous: and Nonnus, in his paraphrase, says, [ ] \"One gave the deadly acid mixed with hyssop.\"</p>\n<p>Jer 8:14; 9:15; 23:15; Mt 27:34,48 vinegar. Mr 15:23,36; Lu 23:36; Joh 19:29,30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-22","title":"Psalms 69:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>Let their table, etc.Or, rather, \"Their table shall become a snare; their eyes shall be darkened,\" etc., in the future tense.</p>\n<p>Pr 1:32; Mal 2:2; Ro 11:8-10 a trap. Isa 8:14,15; 1Pe 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-23","title":"Psalms 69:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>Their eyes. Isa 6:9,10; 29:9,10; Mt 13:14,15; Joh 12:39,40; Ac 28:26,27 Ro 11:25; 2Co 3:14 make their. De 28:65-67; Isa 21:3,4; Jer 30:6; Da 5:6; Ro 11:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-24","title":"Psalms 69:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Pour. 79:6; Le 26:14-46; De 28:15-68; 29:18-28; 31:17; 32:20-26; Ho 5:10 Mt 23:35-37; Lu 21:22; 1Th 2:15,16; Re 16:1 take. Ex 15:15; Isa 13:8; Zec 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-25","title":"Psalms 69:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Let their. 1Ki 9:8; Jer 7:12-14; Mt 23:38; 24:1,2; Ac 1:20 habitation. Heb. palace. Isa 5:1; 6:11 let none dwell. Heb. let there not be a dweller.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-26","title":"Psalms 69:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>For. 109:16; 2Ch 28:9; Job 19:21,22; Zec 1:15; 1Th 2:15 whom. Isa 53:4,10; Zec 13:7 they talk. Mr 15:28-32 those, etc. Heb. thy wounded.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-27","title":"Psalms 69:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>Add. 81:12; Ex 8:15,32; 9:12; Le 26:39; Isa 5:6; Mt 21:19; 23:31,32 Mt 27:4,5; Ro 1:28; 9:18; 2Th 2:11,12; Re 22:10,11 iniquity. or, punishment of iniquity. 109:17-19; 2Ti 4:14 let them. 24:5; Isa 26:10; Ro 9:31; 10:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-28","title":"Psalms 69:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>blotted. Ex 32:32,33; Isa 65:16; Ho 1:9; Re 3:5; 22:19 be written. Isa 4:3; Eze 13:9; Lu 10:20; Php 4:3; Heb 12:23; Re 13:8; 20:12-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-29","title":"Psalms 69:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>I am poor. 40:17; 109:22,31; Isa 53:2,3; Mt 8:20; 2Co 8:9 let thy. 18:48; 22:27-31; 89:26,27; 91:14-16; Eph 1:21,22; Php 2:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-30","title":"Psalms 69:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>I will. 28:7; 40:1-3; 118:21,28,29 magnify. 34:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-31","title":"Psalms 69:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>also shall. 50:13,14,23; Ho 14:2; Eph 5:19,20; Heb 13:15; 1Pe 2:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-32","title":"Psalms 69:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>The humble. or, The meek. 25:9; 34:2; Isa 61:1-3; Joh 16:22; 20:20 your heart. 22:26,29; Isa 55:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-33","title":"Psalms 69:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>the Lord. 10:17; 34:6; 72:12-14; 102:17,20; Isa 66:2; Lu 4:18 his prisoners. 107:10; 146:7; Zec 9:11,12; Ac 5:18,19; 12:4-11; Eph 3:1; Re 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-34","title":"Psalms 69:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>Let. 96:11; 98:7,8; 148:1-14; 150:6; Isa 44:22,23; 49:13; 55:12 Re 7:11-13 moveth. Heb. creepeth. Ge 1:20; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-35","title":"Psalms 69:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>God. 51:18; 102:13,16; 147:12,13; Isa 14:32; 44:26; 46:13; Re 14:1 build. 48:11-13; Eze 36:35,36; Jer 33:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-69-36","title":"Psalms 69:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":69,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":69,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>The seed. 90:16,17; 102:28; Isa 44:3,4; 61:9; Ac 2:39 they. 91:14; Joh 14:23; Ro 8:28; Jas 1:12; 2:5; Re 21:27</p>"}]}